TIP:  So Dwight is playing an electric and not an acoustic so the opening bend of the top string is a little tough to pull off.  You can play either an <f#> on the top string/2nd fret and then just lift off for the <e>, followed by the open 4th string <d>.  Or start with the 4th string/4th fret and slide down to the 2nd fret and then the <d>.

TIP:  There's a distinct strumming cadence which you'll pick up immediately.  But don't play too fast.
 

